env_secrets.s:
Add the secret-reading abstraction used by every server module from here on. ~/AGENTS.md makes this mandatory sitewide: Cloudflare Secrets Store bindings are async objects, plain `[vars]` are strings, and code must never care which it got.

CREATE `src/lib/server/env.ts`:
```ts
export type SecretVal = string | { get?: () => Promise<string> } | undefined;

export async function get_secret(v: SecretVal): Promise<string> {
	if (!v) return '';
	if (typeof v === 'string') return v;
	if (typeof v.get === 'function') return (await v.get()) ?? '';
	return '';
}
```
RULES (from ~/AGENTS.md, non-negotiable): read secrets ONLY via `import { env } from '$env/dynamic/private'`, always through `get_secret(env.KEY)`. Never `env.KEY` as a raw string, never a bare `await env.KEY.get()` at a call site. Local env vars live in `.env` — if a `.dev.vars` ever appears, delete it.

CREATE `.env` (gitignored — confirm `.env` is in `.gitignore`, the scaffold's ignores it already; add it if not) with empty placeholders so local dev boots:
```
SECRET=dev-only-session-secret-change-me
MASTER_KEY=dev-only-32-byte-master-key-change
GOOGLE_ID=
GOOGLE_SECRET=
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY_TEST=
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY_LIVE=
PAYSTACK_TEST=.
HOUSE_BASE_URL=
HOUSE_KEY=
HOUSE_MODEL=
HOUSE_STT_MODEL=
COBALT_URL=
```
`COBALT_URL` is deliberately blank. cobalt's hosted API (`api.cobalt.tools`) is bot-protected and its own docs say do not use it from other projects, and a self-hosted instance still gets blocked by YouTube within days on a datacenter IP. So cobalt is an OPTIONAL escape hatch, never a dependency: when `COBALT_URL` is blank every code path must behave as if cobalt does not exist. The browser extension is the real media-access layer.

