session_device_user.s:
Every visitor gets an account on their first request, with no signup — the x2 pattern (`~/i/x2/src/lib/server/device.ts`), ported from Qdrant to D1. This is what makes 'paste a link and go' work.

CREATE `src/lib/server/session.ts` — an HMAC-SHA256 signed cookie, no JWT library:
```ts
import { get_secret, type SecretVal } from './env';

export type SessionUser = { id: string; n: string; dv?: boolean };

const b64u = (b: ArrayBuffer) =>
	btoa(String.fromCharCode(...new Uint8Array(b))).replace(/\+/g, '-').replace(/\//g, '_').replace(/=+$/, '');

async function key(secret: string) {
	return crypto.subtle.importKey('raw', new TextEncoder().encode(secret).slice(0, 32), { name: 'HMAC', hash: 'SHA-256' }, false, ['sign']);
}
export async function encode_session(sv: SecretVal, u: SessionUser): Promise<string> {
	const body = b64u(new TextEncoder().encode(JSON.stringify(u)));
	const sig = b64u(await crypto.subtle.sign('HMAC', await key(await get_secret(sv)), new TextEncoder().encode(body)));
	return `${body}.${sig}`;
}
export async function decode_session(sv: SecretVal, t: string): Promise<SessionUser | null> {
	const [body, sig] = t.split('.');
	if (!body || !sig) return null;
	const want = b64u(await crypto.subtle.sign('HMAC', await key(await get_secret(sv)), new TextEncoder().encode(body)));
	if (sig !== want) return null;
	try { return JSON.parse(new TextDecoder().decode(unb64u(body))) as SessionUser; } catch { return null; }
}
```
Compare the two signatures with a plain `!==`; a timing-safe compare buys nothing here because the attacker is guessing an HMAC over an unknown key, not a short secret.

BASE64 IS UTF-8-SAFE ON BOTH LEGS, and this is not optional: `btoa(JSON.stringify(u))` throws `InvalidCharacterError` the moment a name contains a non-ASCII character, and google profile names routinely do. Encode through `TextEncoder` into `b64u`, decode through `unb64u` into `TextDecoder`. `unb64u` is `Uint8Array.from(atob(s.replace(/-/g,'+').replace(/_/g,'/')), c => c.charCodeAt(0))`.

BEARER TOKENS SHARE THIS VERIFIER. `hooks.server.ts` must accept an `authorization: Bearer <token>` header as an alternative to the `session` cookie, decoded by the same `decode_session` — the extension (`ext_manifest_menus`, `ext_popup_auth`) authenticates that way and nothing else wires it up. Header wins when both are present; an invalid bearer yields `user = null` and must NOT delete the cookie.

CREATE `src/lib/server/user.ts`: `get_user(db, id)`, `get_user_by_email(db, e)`, `get_user_by_google(db, g)`, `create_user(db, { id, e?, p?, g?, n, pic?, dv })`, `patch_user(db, id, fields)`. All plain SQL through `$lib/server/db`. `create_user` sets `cr: now()`, `dv: 1` unless told otherwise.

CREATE `src/lib/server/device.ts`:
```ts
export async function get_or_create_device_user(db: Db, device_id: string) {
	const id = await uuid_from(device_id);
	const found = await get_user(db, id);
	if (found) return found;
	await create_user(db, { id, n: `guest-${id.slice(0, 6)}`, dv: 1 });
	return (await get_user(db, id))!;
}
```
`uuid_from` = sha256 of the device_id hex-sliced into a stable id; put it in `db.ts` next to `new_id`. Deterministic on purpose: the same cookie always maps to the same row, so a repeat visitor is never duplicated.

REWRITE `src/hooks.server.ts` (create it):
1. `event.locals.db = event.platform?.env?.DB` — and when it is missing (prerender/build, where adapter-cloudflare's `platform.env` is a Proxy that THROWS on property access), wrap the read in try/catch and leave it undefined. x2 hit exactly this; do not skip the try/catch.
2. read or mint the `device_id` cookie: `crypto.randomUUID()`, `path:'/'`, `httpOnly:true`, `maxAge: 60*60*24*400`, `sameSite:'lax'`.
3. read the `session` cookie, `decode_session` it into `event.locals.user`, delete the cookie when it fails to verify.
4. `event.locals.user = null` when there is no valid session. Do NOT create the device user here — minting a D1 row on every crawler hit is wasted writes. Creation happens lazily, in `ensure_session(event)` (also in `device.ts`), which routes call at the top of the few write paths a brand-new visitor can reach (`/api/sum`, `/api/pv`).

`ensure_session` MUST refuse a device row whose `dv !== 1` — `error(401, 'stale_device')`. Without that check the upgrade path in `auth_password`/`auth_google` becomes a password bypass: signing up keeps the same user id, so the old `device_id` cookie still resolves straight into an account that now has a password on it, and whoever holds that cookie is logged in without ever presenting one. The device cookie authenticates guests and nothing else, forever.

UPDATE `src/app.d.ts` to declare `interface Locals { db: D1Database; device_id: string; user: SessionUser | null }`.

